From: xiaoshao9704 <26596822+xiaoshao9704@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: squeezelite: keep custom codec visibility out of dependency graph

The libffmpeg-audio-dec alias now resolves to configurable libffmpeg.
Transitive feature gates make the parent depend on SQUEEZELITE_WMA_ALAC,
while the enclosing if makes that option depend on the parent. Even an
unselected squeezelite-custom then causes a recursive-dependency diagnostic
during make defconfig.

Expose the codec options as an independent menu, as FFmpeg already does
for its own options. A visible-if guard also creates a Kconfig cycle here.
Defaults remain n and no codec or package is selected by this change.

Base: immortalwrt/packages@0a5212e0b37c019df5a152553e571378ec6c5dcc

diff --git a/sound/squeezelite/Makefile b/sound/squeezelite/Makefile
index 9c8fac2..540050a 100644
--- a/sound/squeezelite/Makefile
+++ b/sound/squeezelite/Makefile
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@ define Package/squeezelite-custom
 endef
 
 define Package/squeezelite-custom/config
-	if PACKAGE_squeezelite-custom
+	menu "Squeezelite custom codecs"
 		config SQUEEZELITE_AAC
 		    bool "AAC codec support"
 		    help
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@ define Package/squeezelite-custom/config
 		    help
 			WMA and ALAC codec support
 		    default n
-	endif
+	endmenu
 endef
 
 define Package/squeezelite/description/default
